			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add codegen bridge shape generation and WorkbenchProduct/Progress services\n\nPhase-3 of Wind's VS Code service codegen pipeline: generate\n`Workbench<X>BridgeShape.ts` files as `Pick<...Upstream, ...>`\nover the generated upstream schema, eliminating hand-maintained bridge\nshapes and ensuring upstream API changes surface as TypeScript build\nerrors.\n\nCodegen additions:\n- EmitBridgeShape: Generates `Pick<...>` bridge shape files derived\n  from codegen-emitted upstream schemas\n- EmitBridgeShapeBatch: Batch emitter driven by a curated manifest\n- WorkbenchBridgeShapeManifest: Developer-curated narrowing of which\n  upstream members each Wind service consumes (18 entries)\n- ResolveInterfaceCrossFile: Fallback resolver when interface lives in\n  imported file rather than alongside decorator\n- IterateServiceDecorators: Updated to use cross-file resolution\n- RunCodegen: Orchestrator now runs bridge shape emission after schema\n  generation\n\nNew Wind services:\n- WorkbenchProductService: Bridges IProductService for product metadata\n  (name, version, commit, date, quality, extensionsGallery)\n- WorkbenchProgressService: Bridges IProgressService for progress tasks\n  with location handling (Explorer, Scm, Extensions, Window, etc.)\n\nBoth services follow the established pattern with BridgeShape, Service,\nInterface, Tag, Problem, and Live implementations. LandWorkbenchLayer\nand LandWorkbenchTags updated to include all newly-added services.\n\nprepublishOnly.sh now runs codegen (Stage 1b) before the production\nbuild, ensuring generated schemas + bridge shapes are fresh.",
			"SHA": "5de2328c5a0768bb3bdbff19c0c2f213b87ecefe"
		},
