				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1180,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add codegen emission layer for service schemas and catalog\n\nAdd the code emission layer to Wind's VS Code service codegen pipeline, completing Phase-2 of the system:\n\n- Codegen.ts: Runnable entry point invoked by prepublishOnly.sh\n- RunCodegen.ts: Orchestrator that walks source tree, extracts decorators, emits schemas\n- EmitServiceSchema.ts: Per-service schema emitter - writes `<Decorator>Upstream.ts` files with typed interface members and source-line back-links\n- EmitServiceCatalog.ts: Catalog emitter - writes ServiceCatalog.ts index of all discovered decorators with metadata\n- index.ts: Public exports for library consumers\n\nThe emission layer takes the ServiceDecoratorRecord extraction results from Phase-1 and produces typed TypeScript files under Effect/Generated/ that Wind bridge shapes can import type from. Schema files are idempotent (byte-identical on re-run) with diff-friendly formatting: members sorted by source line, JSDoc preserved verbatim.",
			"SHA": "58dbdc65a57737c1db7bd41cb8f604d37460f347"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T05:07:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1174,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add VS Code service decorator codegen pipeline and global bridge accessor\n\nAdd a new regex-based codegen system that walks the VS Code source tree and extracts `createDecorator(...)` sites along with their interface members:\n\n- `ExtractDecoratorMatch`: Captures decorator export names, tags, and JSDoc from `createDecorator<I<X>>('x')` patterns\n- `ExtractInterfaceMembers`: Extracts typed interface members (properties, methods, events, getters, setters) with parameters and doc comments\n- `IterateServiceDecorators`: Async iterator combining the walkers to yield one `ServiceDecoratorRecord` per decorator\n- `SourceTreeWalker`: Async-iterator over VS Code TypeScript sources, skipping test/build/node_modules directories\n- Typed records: `ServiceDecoratorRecord`, `InterfaceMemberRecord`, `CodegenProblem` ADT for error handling\n\nAlso adds `LandWorkbenchGlobal.ts` - a typed wrapper around `globalThis.__CEL_WIND__` that exposes `CELWind().RunPromise(...)` for Sky consumers without touching the raw global. Dispatches `cel:wind-ready` on installation.\n\nThis infrastructure enables automated Wind-side bridge shape generation from upstream VS Code source, with source-line back-links for traceability.",
			"SHA": "c4fc5b33d7395b7fd41a707edfbcc09b1bbc9eba"
		}
	],
